lattice3dshell_lle_twist_n4.out
Shell-mode lattice3d twist verification (latticelinearelastic, nLayers=4): torsion must match the nLayers=1 plate value, confirming per-layer self-J plus the automatic shear-offset Steiner (no double count).
StaticStructural nsteps 3 rtolv 1.e-6 ddm 4 2 1 2 4 ddv 2 1.e-4 1.e-3 ddltf 2 nmodules 1
errorcheck
domain 3dLattice
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all element_all
ndofman 2 nelem 1 ncrosssect 1 nmat 1 nbc 1 nic 0 nltf 2
node 1 coords 3 0.000000e+00 0.000000e+00 0.000000e+00 bc 6 1 1 1 1 1 1
node 2 coords 3 1.000000e+00 0.000000e+00 0.000000e+00 bc 6 0 0 0 0 0 0
lattice3D 1 nodes 2 1 2 crossSect 1 mat 1 shellnormal 3 0.0 0.0 1.0 polycoords 12 0.5 -0.05 -0.005   0.5 0.05 -0.005   0.5 0.05 0.005   0.5 -0.05 0.005
latticecs 1 material 1 nlayers 4
latticelinearelastic 1 d 2400. tAlpha 0.0 e 30.e9 a1 0.5 a2 1.0 a3 0.5
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 prescribedvalue 0.0
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1.
PiecewiseLinFunction 2 nPoints 2 t 2 1. 4. f(t) 2 0. 1.
#%BEGIN_CHECK% tolerance 1.e-3
## Multi-layer twist must reproduce the nLayers=1 plate torsion (see
## lattice3dshell_lle.in) bit-for-bit.
## Reaction node 1 dof 1 = axial   = -E*eps*A   = -2.0000e3   N
## Reaction node 1 dof 4 = torsion = -G*J*twist = -8.3333e-2  N*m
## With the per-layer self-torsion J_layer = b*dh^3/12 the plate twisting comes
## from the layer shear forces acting at their through-thickness offset:
## G*Sum(A_k*y_k^2) (Steiner) + G*Sum(b*dh^3/12) (self) = G*b*t^3/12 exactly.
## The pre-fix code (J_layer = b*t^3/12 / nLayers) re-added the full plate J on
## every layer on top of the automatic shear Steiner and gave ~-1.6667e-1.
#REACTION tStep 3 number 1 dof 1 value -2.0000e+3
#REACTION tStep 3 number 1 dof 4 value -8.3333e-2
#%END_CHECK%
